## 🌐 Build a Website in TechScript (New in v2!)

No HTML. No CSS. No JavaScript files. Just one `.txs` file:

```techscript
use web

make page = WebPage("My First Website")

page.style("body", {
    "background": "#0f0f11",
    "color": "#eee",
    "font-family": "sans-serif",
    "text-align": "center",
    "padding": "60px"
})

page.script("""
    function greet() {
        alert('Hello from TechScript!');
    }
""")

page.body([
    page.h1("Welcome to TechScript"),
    page.p("No HTML. No CSS. No build steps. Just TechScript."),
    page.button("Say Hello", { "onclick": "greet()" })
])

page.run()
```

Run it:
```bash
tech run my_site.txs
```

**Your browser opens automatically!** 🚀

---

## 📝 Language at a Glance

```techscript
# Hello World
say "Hello, World!"

# Variables
make name = "Alice"
keep MAX = 100

# Input
make answer = ask "What is your name? "
say f"Hello, {answer}!"

# Conditions
when name == "Alice" {
    say "Welcome, Alice!"
} else {
    say f"Who are you, {name}?"
}

# Loops
each i in 1..5 {
    say f"Count: {i}"
}

# Functions
build greet(name, msg = "Hello") {
    say f"{msg}, {name}!"
}
greet("Bob")

# Classes
model Dog {
    build init(self, name) {
        self.name = name
    }
    build speak(self) {
        say f"{self.name} says Woof!"
    }
}
make rex = Dog("Rex")
rex.speak()

# Error handling
attempt {
    say 1 / 0
} catch err {
    say "Caught error!"
}
```

---

## 🛠️ All CLI Commands

```bash
tech run <file.txs>          # Run a TechScript file
tech run <file.txs> --debug  # Run with debug output
tech check <file.txs>        # Check for syntax errors
tech repl                    # Interactive REPL shell
tech transpile <file.txs>    # Convert to Python
tech version                 # Show version
```

